// 010 — Print current date and time — DESIGN NOTE
// "Get the current wall-clock time" is a syscall on every Unix:
//   clock_gettime(CLOCK_REALTIME, &ts) → seconds since 1970 + nanos.
//
// AiLang's compile-time syscall dispatch (Library.CSysDispatch) knows
// the syscall numbers, but the user-facing wrapper — a `Library.Time`
// with `Time_Now() -> Integer` and helpers to break apart epoch
// seconds into Y/M/D h:m:s — isn't here yet.
//
// When it lands, this demo gets rewritten to call Time_Now() and
// FormatLocalTime(). Until then, the placeholder shows the *shape*
// of what the API will look like.
SubRoutine.Main {
    // Hard-coded sample to illustrate the eventual call shape:
    epoch_seconds = 1714530000      // arbitrary fixed timestamp
    PrintMessage("epoch seconds (mock) = ")
    PrintNumber(epoch_seconds)
    PrintMessage("\n")
    PrintMessage("(real Time_Now() will arrive with Library.Time)\n")
}
RunTask(Main)
